WEBVTT

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.430
Ta-da~a!

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.540
By my authority as a GOTT ES member,

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.880
I charge you with being interstellar criminals.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.840
Chief, request authorization to execute an arrest.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:20.910
This way!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:24.910
Listen up! I do not recognize you thugs as having the right to remain silent,

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.580
or the right to call an attorney!

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.980
Inspector...

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:37.860
Finally, finally, we have Drake in custody. Congratulations.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.190
So you might say, but after pursuing him this far out into the frontier,

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.420
so far out, that in order to get approval from the chief, the time lag...

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.870
<i>Éclair-san...?</i>

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.540
...lasted this long!

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:57.370
Even so, now you can return back to Aineias triumphantly,

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.540
so what does it matter?

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:02.550
That's all very well, <i>if</i> we are able to return safely.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:07.890
So then, Éclair, Lumiere, I'll be awaiting your safe return.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.150
We will come back right away.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.390
Planet No. 2 Commuter ferry two-zero-one

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:20.230
has arrived three minutes behind schedule.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:23.900
Flights headed to Borgall via the Warp Gate...

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:28.570
These are our current coordinates in the Colce system, in Perseus' arm.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.180
We cannot use your ships to get us to the galactic central judiciary offices,

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.510
due to that outfit that he's bundled up in.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.880
We can't take that guy aboard.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.850
He sticks out higher than the La Muse's payload deck all by himself.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:49.190
Even a villain who has committed 1024 cases of fraud is afraid of death.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:52.860
It appears that he believes in the god named "Health."

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.870
How is he any different from a cyborg?

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.500
He's preserving his purity as an original Earth-based human.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.490
Or so he says.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:09.210
We'll take this ship to turn him in to the galactic central judiciary offices.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.550
What ship?

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:14.810
It's an AP-D330, an armored destroyer, is it not?

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.520
I've got permission from above.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.050
Things have been pretty dangerous lately, after all.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.900
I'm sorry, Wirbelwind.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.670
Your body is just too slim.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.550
Although we'll be apart, we'll still be together.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.340
Okay then, I'll be going...

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:06.200
This is a precision machine, that gives me life!

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.210
If you do anything to cause a malfunction,

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.210
I will sue the judicial office! Got that?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.540
If you're as spirited as all this, that should be enough, right?

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:18.220
Who do you think I am, boy? I am Drake Han!

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.890
You just get ready for when they assign you to some do-nothing post!

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.890
Right, right...

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.450
Are you Inspectors coming along too?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:31.260
Things have been pretty dangerous lately, after all...

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.170
Have you done something to make him dislike you?

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.500
Mm-mm. Never mind that, have you finished saying goodbye?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:44.510
Yes. But it's not as though we were tossing the La Muse aside.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:49.180
Proximity cordon, 3-by-3, clear! No obstacle targets.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.520
There sure are a lot of people moving to Y-E Shift, huh?

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.850
There sure are.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:58.190
Excuse me, <i>Armbrust-san,</i> but are you sure this is all right?

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.190
What do you mean?

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:03.860
Those two. <i>ES members.</i>

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:08.530
If I had to say, they're GOTT's illegal activities personnel, right?

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.200
To have public servants, who should be just, mixed up in such illegality...

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.340
to say nothing of whether those children are fit to be serving

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.870
as agents of the law...

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:20.210
They're not illegal, they're <i>extra-</i> legal activities.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.610
And besides, between adults and children, if anything,

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.550
it's probably the children who are more pure.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:29.590
However, you are under orders from the Global Union

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.820
to watch over their activities, aren't you?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.430
If they were to act under my supervision,

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:41.860
those girls would be special S-Class wanted criminals by now.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.970
I can hear every word they're saying!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.780
Attention, attention, Warp Gate transit routes

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.510
A-04 through H-21 to the center of the galaxy...

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.150
...will have their schedules delayed due to an accident.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.850
Details are as follows...

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.520
What do they mean!?

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.790
He's saying that our syncing up to the gate

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.860
to the center of the galaxy will be a bit delayed.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:09.890
Waiting is also part of the job.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:13.200
Or are you worried about being late for a TV show you want to watch?

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.370
I never said anything like that!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.200
The prisoner's delivery schedule is of the highest priority!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.210
I thought I told you that beforehand...

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.540
What is it?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.740
A change in plans. If we're going to be made to wait here,

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:30.550
then let's take another route, even if it's longer, to the galaxy center.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.150
That's crazy!

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:36.150
It's not crazy! As the GOTT person responsible for escorting them-

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.820
I'm against it.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:41.520
As the person in charge on the Colce side, I'm against it.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.860
There have been instances where plans were not carefully changed,

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.160
and right after slipping into the Warp Gate,

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.500
a fleet of <i>Insurer</i> attack ships was there, lying in wait.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.500
Insurer?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:57.370
They're a group that makes their living by raiding prisoner transport ships.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.710
I've heard of them too.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:04.480
It's like life insurance for the underworld.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:07.520
Apparently, by paying them a certain premium,

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.520
you can have them abduct you from a prisoner transport ship.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.020
They're a notorious bunch. Particularly around here.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.700
Attention, attention, now updating latest schedules for Warp Gate

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.530
transit routes A-04 through H-21, to the center of the galaxy.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.870
Currently, at Galactic Standard Time 23:30, routes via Machia and Borgall...

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:29.540
l- Inspector, Where are you going?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.780
We're getting nowhere talking over the monitors!

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.840
I'm going to file a protest with the administration office directly!

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:37.200
Excellent work, sir!

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:46.880
"No Admittance"

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.160
Damn...

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.830
It'll be a three-hour wait after all, huh?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:54.290
And if those <i>Insurers</i> make their move during that time...

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.440
How about some coffee, <i>Inspector-san?</i>

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:03.170
<i>Éclair-cha... - san...</i>

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:05.840
That's okay. I don't like coffee.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:08.170
Well then, tea?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.940
I'll have some.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:20.190
Inspector, you don't like me, do you?

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:22.860
As far as our duties go, it doesn't matter, does it?

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.400
Since we're here together on the same mission,

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.860
I'd like to get along with you at least a little bit.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:32.140
All we need to do is fulfill our duties. This isn't a sightseeing tour.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:36.870
Oh? Even though once I leave here, I may never come back?

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.610
Don't say such a thing.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:50.150
Thanks for the tea. It was good.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:54.250
Inspector, please wait! I haven't finished mine yet.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:02.520
Pops here lost his wife and daughter earlier.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.100
At the time,

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:09.170
someone involved with the suspect in the case he was on took them hostage,

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.510
and ever since then, he's been all...

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:11.840
Now, see here!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.180
Enough of that inane chatter. I'd rather you not misunderstand me.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:20.850
I'm not after revenge or anything. It's just that, as a policeman,

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.410
I detest criminal activity.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.530
I'm still a child, so I may not understand too well,

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:32.130
but the law is not something that's there to exert control over people,

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:35.130
it's something that's there to protect them.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.390
Right?

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.150
There's something abnormal about the ship passing through 0-0. It's hostile!

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.520
The Insurers?

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.500
There's a consort ship stacked up!

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.160
I can't fire!

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:18.510
What's the matter?

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:22.510
They're in the beam gun's blind spot! There are ten more of them!

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.000
Now what!?

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:29.850
The ten hostile units attached to the main ship have all exploded...

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.190
They what!?

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.860
Please excuse me.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.190
I was a bit slow dealing with them.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.870
Are we all right?

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:47.200
The armor plating is okay, but the paint has been scratched off.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.800
You two?

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.210
What are you doing!? After the hostile mother ship!

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.440
The hostile mother ship appears to be secure.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:06.620
59AP3258775, you are behind schedule. Please proceed to the Warp Gate.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.760
Okay then, past the gate is out of our jurisdiction.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.900
We can only escort you this far. We hope you have a safe trip.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:19.430
Roger. Have the criminal reports in order for me when I get back.

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:27.580
Right then, from here on it's just us and this ship.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.940
It would be nice if those earlier guys were the only Insurers there were...

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.510
Okay, course field clear.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.250
The large ship is next.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:46.490
I'm reading a fluctuation in mass...

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:50.530
Never mind, it's within prescribed values. No problems.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:53.200
What are you doing!? On to the next one!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.800
Okay! Course field clear...

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.250
Displaying countdown to Warp-out.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.570
If everything goes smoothly, we'll be at the center of the galaxy in three hours.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.570
<i>If</i> everything goes smoothly.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.570
Have all stations check in, and report status.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.910
Warp-in status check.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.900
Condition is "all green." No trouble.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.520
Hey, how about it?

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:47.350
It'll do. These sensors will be a cinch.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:54.860
Get out.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:58.540
Use this. It's not much of a weapon, but still...

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.200
You guys are the Insurers?

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:05.540
Yeah. We also moonlight as cops.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.770
This can't be possible...

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.180
Excuse me.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:18.920
Well, well, this is a delicate job.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:22.560
All of the key circuits have been physically cut all over.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.120
This can't be!

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.290
<i>Wirbelwind...</i>

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.840
This is impossible! Traitors!?

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.210
I have heard rumors about there being crooked cops,

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:41.180
but I never thought they'd be this close!

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.170
Smith!

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.860
With guns as simple as these, we won't have to call on Lumiere, will we?

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.190
Dammit!

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.560
Watch out!

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.860
Were you worried about me?

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:01.200
You hush!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.220
Thanks, Inspector!

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:15.880
Fall back! Fall back to where <i>Drake-sama</i> is at once!

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:17.370
Hold it!

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:21.220
Are you okay, Smith?

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:26.560
I'm all right, Inspector. I'm sorry, please go on!

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.220
Hang in there.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:31.490
Take care of him!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.160
Sorry, let's go!

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.650
Right!

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:38.830
You mean you were lying when you said that was life support equipment!?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:42.500
It <i>is</i> equipment necessary for sustaining my life, as you'll see.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:46.830
It's a cluster of weapons that can pass any scan.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.180
What sort of stunt is this?

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:58.050
In accordance with your contract with the Insurers, <i>Drake-san,</i>

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:01.850
we have retrieved your person from the authorities.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:05.320
However, our company has taken on a new duty, you see.

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:09.190
We have been solicited to carry out your murder.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:14.130
W- who did this? I know, it was Red, right?

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.200
But he's been long since taken care of...

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.130
It's the code of the business...

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.540
our duty is to protect such privileged information.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.210
We will not make the identity of our client known.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:26.540
Not even if they <i>have</i> happened to have passed away.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:30.210
It looks like your life support equipment wasn't enough, huh?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.320
When you're reincarnated,

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.490
you should come back as a rat in an arms depot or something!

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.010
Why, you!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:49.170
<i>You're still alive, then? I see!</i>

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:50.260
<i>All right!</i>

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:54.170
Approaching Warp-out...

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.140
Now entering Warp-out...

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:07.580
Oh, my! There aren't very many stars.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:09.850
We've been flung to quite a frontier stellar region, huh?

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.790
I'm picking up multiple readings around us.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:13.190
We're surrounded by an armada!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:16.650
The Insurer armada, huh? It's a fairly large one.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.200
They're here to meet the group from earlier.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.560
Or, in the event of failure,

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:24.530
then they're for all of us together, aren't they?

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:26.200
Can you raise shields?

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.000
The circuits have been torn to pieces!

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:44.820
An enemy ship has exploded! And another...

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:54.700
You don't have to apologize, Wirbelwind.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:58.690
The armor on this ship is tougher than I thought.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:08.850
There's nothing on the physical sensors! Does it have a powerful Canceller?

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.510
Let them have it as hard as you can, Lumiere!

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:13.680
Like she said, Wirbelwind!

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:38.800
That ship... it's yours?

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:45.810
Well done! You even hid it from the Warp Gate and fooled them!

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:49.880
We girls should be elegant.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:02.270
We've received a transmission.

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:04.170
It seems there was a staffer at the Warp Gate administration office...

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.940
...that had his family taken hostage,

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.370
and he's the one who sent us all the way out here.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:13.180
Your... your body...

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:17.850
It looks like you've had prohibited technologies applied to you.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:22.850
So, you don't like unlawful girls after all?

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:28.050
If there's anyone that doesn't like you, I'll arrest them for you!

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:39.140
Okay then, we will escort Drake in the La Muse.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:42.470
Knowing you two, you're probably all right, but be careful.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:45.480
Things have been pretty dangerous lately, after all.

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:47.480
You're worried about us?

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:51.810
Yeah, I'm worried. I couldn't stand to see anything dangerous happen to you!

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.440
Thanks, Inspector!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.830
As it happens, if I could get you to pay

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.500
what those in the business are asking for you,

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:17.030
I would almost be willing to take responsibility for letting you get away...

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.440
But if you're disinclined,

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:24.940
then we should just consider you and me to be out of luck, and abandon the idea.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:32.880
Hey! Just a minute! Come back here! Hey! Hey! Come on! Hey! Hey, come back!

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:09.060
<i>The pounding of the heart marks time.</i>

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Although it may accelerate, it never stops.</i>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:15.970
<i>The meaning of the word "stop" is death.</i>

00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:19.800
<i>Next time on Kiddy Grade</i>
